    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d509">

                <pb facs="0535" n="523" sameAs="frus:frus1945v08/pg523"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">761.91/1–1145</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum by the Director of the Office of Near Eastern
                        wad African Affairs</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Murray</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1944-12-30">December 30, 1944</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>I concur fully that it would be preferable for the matter of the Iranian Railway
                    and free port to be discussed with the President, and I hope you will have an
                    early opportunity to do so. I am afraid, if the matter is delayed, that the
                    President may feel that adequate attention is not being paid to his suggestion
                    that Harriman take up the matter with Stalin.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Wallace Murray</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
